The PPA workflow prepares one source branch for Launchpad, as in Corium.
No compilation or GPG signing happens in GitHub Actions. The generated
build/ppa branch exists only in Launchpad's arma-ppa repository.

Use the arma recipe, with daily builds disabled, targeting ppa:nmccallum/pichi:

    # git-build-recipe format 0.4 deb-version {debversion}+{time}
    lp:~nmccallum/pichi-vm/+git/arma-ppa build/ppa

Select Resolute, Stonking and Tenacious, the Ubuntu guest releases with
kernel 7.0 or newer, and enable amd64 and arm64 in the PPA. Arma is a guest
image tool; it does not need a Noble host package.

Ubuntu lacks prebuilt Rust libraries for Tatu's bare-metal targets. The
package builds core from the release's rust-src, then builds Arma with
that private bare-metal sysroot and the distro's normal host libraries.
Source preparation vendors both Rust 1.93 and 1.97 library dependencies
alongside Cargo.lock dependencies, so the same branch builds offline on
these releases. Update the source-package list when their Rust series changes.

LAUNCHPAD_AUTHORIZATION is the repository OAuth header secret, as in Corium.
Each main push publishes source and requests recipe builds. CI finishes
when Launchpad accepts the request; building and publication continue there.
